note DIT probe: prints "hwdit N" (1: FEAT_DIT advertised by the kernel, 0: not, -1: auxv unreadable)
note and exits 0 when N is 0 or 1, 1 otherwise. The expectation on a GB10 (Cortex-X925 / A725) is 1;
note dit.sh compares it with /proc/cpuinfo.
text dmsg "hwdit "
fn main to int
o = new uchar 16 0
v = tls_hwdit
k = ulong 0
if lt v 0
put o 0 45
k = 1
v = neg v
end
put o k add 48 uchar v
put o add k 1 10
w = write 1 dmsg 0 len dmsg
w = write 1 o 0 add k 2
if or lt v 0 gt v 1
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
